## Best Practices

### State Management

- Use `this.setState()` to update agent state rather than modifying `this.state` directly
- Define a type for your agent's state to ensure type safety
- Set `initialState` in your agent class for default state values
- Implement `onStateUpdate` to react to state changes from all sources

### AI Integration

- Use the AI SDK (@ai-sdk/openai, @ai-sdk/anthropic, etc.) for structured interaction with AI models
- Store API keys in Durable Objects for user-specific keys
- Use environment secrets for default/fallback API keys
- Always handle API errors and provide fallbacks for AI services

### Performance

- Minimize token usage by crafting efficient prompts
- Use smaller models for simpler tasks to reduce latency and cost
- Implement caching strategies for frequently requested information
- Use streaming responses for better user experience
- Use `stepCountIs()` to limit tool call iterations

### Security

- Validate all user inputs before processing
- Implement authentication for agent connections via `onBeforeConnect`
- Use Better Auth for session management
- Apply rate limiting to prevent abuse
- Never expose API keys to the client
